213
00:15:05,595 --> 00:15:06,523
Let's land this.

214
00:15:06,863 --> 00:15:11,138
The summary has four parts: what happened,
the root cause with its layer, what was

215
00:15:11,178 --> 00:15:14,138
done and how it was verified,
and what prevents a repeat.

216
00:15:14,478 --> 00:15:19,147
Never write "verified" for a check that
was not run, and always state what is not

217
00:15:19,187 --> 00:15:19,903
yet verified.

218
00:15:20,243 --> 00:15:26,149
Every line of a timeline carries its source:
a reflog entry, a tag, a log line, a

219
00:15:26,189 --> 00:15:26,736
message.

220
00:15:27,076 --> 00:15:31,928
A postmortem is blameless so that it
explains the system and so that people keep

221
00:15:31,968 --> 00:15:35,414
handing over evidence; replace
names by roles to test it.

222
00:15:35,754 --> 00:15:40,165
A control is ranked by what enforces it,
from "the server refuses" down to habit,

223
00:15:40,205 --> 00:15:43,847
and it comes with an owner, a date
and a way to know that it works.

224
00:15:45,687 --> 00:15:51,224
